Alternative for GRA-07: normalise Matrix Market indices to base 0 while
reading (store sorttab vertnum - baseval) and work in unbased space,
adding baseval only when writing verttax/edgetax, so the fill loop
compares unbased index against mrownbr. Cleaner model but rewrites many
lines of a rarely used converter; larger regression risk than the
two-token bound fix. (Representative hunk; a full implementation touches
the read loop, the sort comparison and both verttax writers.)

--- a/src/libscotch/graph_io_mmkt.c
+++ b/src/libscotch/graph_io_mmkt.c
@@ -202,3 +202,3 @@
   for (sortnum = degrmax = 0, vertnum = verttmp = baseval - 1, edgetmp = edgenum = baseval;
        sortnum < sortnbr; sortnum ++) {
     Gnum                vertend;
@@ -227,3 +227,3 @@
-  while (vertnum < mrownbr)                       /* Fill gaps with isolated vertices */
+  while ((vertnum - baseval) < (mrownbr - 1))     /* Fill gaps with isolated vertices (unbased compare) */
     grafptr->verttax[++ vertnum] = edgenum;
